{"agent":"fx-glob-waits","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new filters exclude any item whose `terminal` flag is true from `state.active_leases(...)` when detecting glob clashes. An item can be finished while its lease is still unreleased and still returned by `state.active_leases(...)`, so this change resolves that still-held contention automatically when the item finishes. The default in [D-lease-break-explicit] is that an active held lease is broken only through `ddflow claim --break`; this makes finished items effective implicit breaks.","digest":"324ca85d6a7f896c","location":"[D-lease-break-explicit] ddflow/services/leases.py:_clash_text (also the new `live=` filter around line 181)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"[D-lease-break-explicit] ddflow/services/leases.py:_clash_text (also the new `live=` filter around line 181)"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"When every requested glob is kept as a conflict, `keep == []`. The surrounding message does not guard that case, so for input `globs=[\"docs/**\"]` it renders `\"drop the overlapping ones ( would be accepted)\"` — a false parenthetical because no requested glob would be accepted. The user-facing instruction is wrong in exactly the all-globs-conflict case.","digest":"70ecb4481c062c00","location":"ddflow/services/leases.py:update_lease","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/leases.py:update_lease"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":8137,"diff_sha":"e6c4409325750e3703753367579bb567650ccadf2f1a3fd728efe9e11e8b8248","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":966.0,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"a168a08d033b3094","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-shared-glob-update-waits.critic.lan-deepseek-