{"agent":"fx-glob-waits","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The filter keeps a `pairs` entry whenever any actual changed path matches the requested glob, but it never checks whether that path is covered by a `shared_globs(cfg)` pattern. Example: config shared `docs/README.md`; other lease is `docs/**`; user requests `docs/**`; `conflicts([\"docs/**\"], [\"docs/**\"], shared)` still returns `(\"docs/**\", \"docs/**\")` because the two globs overlap on non-shared paths, and the other holder's only changed path is `docs/README.md`. `any(GL.match(p, a) for p in changed)` is true for the shared README, so `_clash_text` returns a clash and refuses the update even though the only real change is an exempt shared file. Shared files should be inert for overlap, just as they already are when `conflicts` decides the glob pair in the first place.","digest":"6f5804597008660d","location":"ddflow/services/leases.py:_clash_text changed-path filter","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/leases.py:_clash_text changed-path filter"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"[D-lease-break-explicit] Filtering terminal items out of `live` means a live, unreleased lease on a finished item no longer counts as contention: `_clash_text`/`glob_clash` will return no clash for an overlapping update without `ddflow claim --break`. That makes lease breaking implicit in the contended/idle case that this decision says must remain explicit by default (`break_on_timeout` defaults to false); the automatic mode should only come from config.","digest":"7a190ec88aaefe24","location":"ddflow/services/leases.py:live filtering in glob_clash/_clash_text","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/leases.py:live filtering in glob_clash/_clash_text"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":8741,"diff_sha":"c7787770eeca6e60a938c5885ae4e84e8523e8dd70c99941dbd994bb51c171e3","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked work